  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "contrasts",
  "title": "Which did you hear?",
  "description": "Sounds English speakers mix up in Indonesian: full vowels in every syllable, c that's always 'ch', and a tapped r against l. Hear a word and pick which one it was.",
  "sets": [
    {
      "id": "vowels",
      "sound": "Full vowels: a, i, u",
      "note": "Indonesian has no weak syllables: every a, i and u keeps its full sound, where English would blur some to 'uh'. Listen to each vowel, the last one especially, and say it as clearly as the first: bata ends in 'ah', batu in 'oo'.",
